<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithms</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section,
we itemize the algorithm pseudocodes of the MakGIT sampler (<a href="#alg1" title="In Appendix A Algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
Moment Sampler (<a href="#alg2" title="In Appendix A Algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and the general form of choose-then-sample methods (<a href="#alg3" title="In Appendix A Algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> One-round of MaskGIT sampler: <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{OneRoundMaskGIT}((p_{i})_{i\in I},k,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>OneRoundMaskGIT</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{OneRoundMaskGIT}((p_{i})_{i\in I},k,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>: Family of probability distributions over <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert I\rvert=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert I\rvert=N</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of indices to choose

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: Gumbel temperature

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in I^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in I^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> distinct indices

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>: Sampled tokens

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          Independently sample <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\sim p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\sim p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          Independently sample standard Gumbel noise <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\leftarrow\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in I}\{\log p_{i}(x_{i})+\alpha\xi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>argtop</mi><mo lspace="0.130em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\leftarrow\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in I}\{\log p_{i}(x_{i})+\alpha\xi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> One-round of Moment sampler: <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{OneRoundMoment}((p_{i})_{i\in I},k,\alpha,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>OneRoundMoment</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{OneRoundMoment}((p_{i})_{i\in I},k,\alpha,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>: Family of probability distributions over <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert I\rvert=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert I\rvert=N</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of indices to choose

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: Gumbel temperature, with <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:=1+1/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:=1+1/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: Inverse sampling temperature (set <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\beta</annotation></semantics></math> when approximating MaskGIT)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in I^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in I^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> distinct indices

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>: Sampled tokens

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          Independently sample standard Gumbel noise <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\leftarrow\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in I}\{\log\bigl(\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)^{\beta}\bigr)+\xi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>argtop</mi><mo lspace="0.130em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\leftarrow\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in I}\{\log\bigl(\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)^{\beta}\bigr)+\xi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
          Independently sample <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i_{\ell}}\sim p_{i_{\ell}}^{\gamma}/\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\gamma}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i_{\ell}}\sim p_{i_{\ell}}^{\gamma}/\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\gamma}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[k]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> General choose-then-sample algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot|I,\bm{x}_{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot|I,\bm{x}_{I})</annotation></semantics></math>: Distribution over nonempty subsets of <math id="alg3.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[D]\setminus I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[D]\setminus I</annotation></semantics></math>
conditioned by <math id="alg3.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg3.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})</annotation></semantics></math>: Dimension-wise denoising model for any <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,I,\bm{x}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,I,\bm{x}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: Inverse sampling temperature

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\mathcal{S}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\mathcal{S}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>: Generated sample

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subsetneq[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊊</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subsetneq[D]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J\sim\pi(\cdot|I,\bm{x}_{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\sim\pi(\cdot|I,\bm{x}_{I})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Ignore <math id="alg3.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\emptyset}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\emptyset}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="alg3.l9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{j}\sim\frac{p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})^{\gamma}}{\lVert p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\rVert^{\gamma}_{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{j}\sim\frac{p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})^{\gamma}}{\lVert p_{j|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\rVert^{\gamma}_{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg3.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg3.l10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{I\cup J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{I\cup J}</annotation></semantics></math> has been determined so far
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\leftarrow I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\leftarrow I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Informal derivation of moment sampler</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive the moment sampler approximation (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)
from (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
First, by applying the approximation (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) to (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
we have</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{t}^{*}=i_{t}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{t-1}^{*}=i_{t-1},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\approx\frac{p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{t}^{*}=i_{t}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{t-1}^{*}=i_{t-1},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\approx\frac{p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by multiplying this for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\approx\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\approx\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that the right-hand side is independent of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so we can replace the conditioning on <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
By marginalizing out <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I_{\ell-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I_{\ell-1}</annotation></semantics></math> from this, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{i_{1}}}\cdots\sum_{x_{i_{\ell-1}}}\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid(x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell}}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell-1}}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></munder></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{i_{1}}}\cdots\sum_{x_{i_{\ell-1}}}\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid(x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell}}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i\in I_{\ell-1}}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\left(\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{\sum_{x_{i_{t}}}p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\right)\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\left(\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{\sum_{x_{i_{t}}}p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i_{t}}(x_{i_{t}})}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\right)\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{\lVert p_{i_{t}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\right)}_{=:C_{\ell-1}(i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1})}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\prod_{t=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{\lVert p_{i_{t}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{t-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\right)}_{=:C_{\ell-1}(i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1})}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(x_{i_{\ell}},i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)=\frac{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left(x_{i_{\ell}}\right)}{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(x_{i_{\ell}},i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)=\frac{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid x_{i_{\ell}}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left(x_{i_{\ell}}\right)}{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\approx\frac{C_{\ell-1}(i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1})}{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\propto\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.278em">≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\approx\frac{C_{\ell-1}(i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1})}{\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1}\right)}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\propto\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Since the final right-hand side is actually a normalized probability distribution over <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\times([N]\setminus I_{\ell-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\times([N]\setminus I_{\ell-1})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have derived (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Strategy for formal proof of <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2 (Moment sampler approximates MaskGIT in the 𝑁≫𝑘^2 regime). ‣ Moment sampler. ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, we work under the following setting:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmsett1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_sett">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmsett1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setting A</span></span><span id="Thmsett1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MaskGIT sampler)<span id="Thmsett1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmsett1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmsett1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmsett1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We are given <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> probability distributions <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> over a finite set <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We sample <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\sim p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\sim p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and standard Gumbel noise <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independently for each <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let
<math id="Thmsett1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{*}_{1},\ldots,i^{*}_{k})=\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in[N]}\{\log p_{i}(x_{i})+\alpha\xi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>argtop</mi><mo lspace="0.130em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{*}_{1},\ldots,i^{*}_{k})=\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in[N]}\{\log p_{i}(x_{i})+\alpha\xi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="Thmsett1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us start by applying Bernstein’s inequality (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boucheron et al. 2013, Corollary 2.11</a></cite>)
to the sum of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the summand is always within <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
for <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\leq-t\right)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2(\sigma^{2}+t/3)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\leq-t\right)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2(\sigma^{2}+t/3)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}:=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}:=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Now, recall that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]=\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\right]=\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1+1/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1+1/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
By letting <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\epsilon\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\epsilon\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>
and combining (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>),
we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\leq(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}\leq(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)^{2}}{2(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}+\epsilon\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}/3)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)^{2}}{2(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}+\epsilon\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}/3)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)}{2(1+\epsilon/3)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)}{2(1+\epsilon/3)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To utilize this estimate for our analysis of MaskGIT sampler,
we prove the following proposition.
The proof is given in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#Thmsett1" title="Setting A (MaskGIT sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Setting</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>,
let <math id="Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]_{&lt;k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]_{&lt;k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of all the subsets of <math id="Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]</annotation></semantics></math> with cardinality less than <math id="Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for <math id="Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\quad\text{for all $I\in[N]_{&lt;k}$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.000em;" width="1.000em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\quad\text{for all $I\in[N]_{&lt;k}$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with probability at least
<math id="Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We use <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to prove the following assertion,
whose proof is given in <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5</span></span><span id="Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#Thmsett1" title="Setting A (MaskGIT sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Setting</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>,
assume <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
For <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, let us define <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\subset\mathcal{S}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\subset\mathcal{S}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of
<math id="Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the following inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad&lt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.278em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad&lt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\ell-1}:=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\ell-1}:=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We next compute the probability distribution of the moment sampler.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmsett2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_sett">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmsett2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setting B</span></span><span id="Thmsett2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moment sampler)<span id="Thmsett2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmsett2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmsett2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmsett2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We are given <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> probability distributions
<math id="Thmsett2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
over a finite set <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1+1/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1+1/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
We sample <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\sim p_{i}^{\beta}/\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\sim p_{i}^{\beta}/\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>
and standard Gumbel noise <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independently for each <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j_{1}^{*},\ldots,j_{k}^{*})=\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in[N]}\{\log\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}+\eta_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>argtop</mi><mo lspace="0.130em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j_{1}^{*},\ldots,j_{k}^{*})=\operatorname{argtop\hskip 1.25pt{\it k}}_{i\in[N]}\{\log\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}+\eta_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmsett2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6</span></span><span id="Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#Thmsett2" title="Setting B (Moment sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Setting</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, for each distinct indices <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>
and (not necessarily distinct) <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i_{1}},\ldots,z_{i_{k}}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i_{1}},\ldots,z_{i_{k}}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\ell-1}:=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\ell-1}:=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is given in <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Let us finally prove <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2 (Moment sampler approximates MaskGIT in the 𝑁≫𝑘^2 regime). ‣ Moment sampler. ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The following is its restatement under the above settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7</span></span><span id="Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Setting <a href="#Thmsett1" title="Setting A (MaskGIT sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> &amp; <a href="#Thmsett2" title="Setting B (Moment sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>,
for each <math id="Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{i}=(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in[N]^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{i}=(i_{1},\ldots,i_{k})\in[N]^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
let</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(x_{i_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(x_{i_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, as probability distributions over <math id="Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]^{k}\times\mathcal{S}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]^{k}\times\mathcal{S}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}({p}_{\mathrm{moment}},{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq 5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(1+\sqrt{\log^{+}\!\left(\frac{N}{k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}\right)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}({p}_{\mathrm{moment}},{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq 5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(1+\sqrt{\log^{+}\!\left(\frac{N}{k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}}\right)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log^{+}(x):=\log(\max\{1,x\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log^{+}(x):=\log(\max\{1,x\})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This main result is proven in <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3 (One-by-one CTS algorithm is unbiased). ‣ Choose-then-sample algorithms. ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{0}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{0}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and inductively (and randomly) define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{n}\sim\pi(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}}),\qquad x_{\sigma_{n}}\sim p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}}),\qquad I_{n}:=I_{n-1}\cup\{\sigma_{n}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}\sim\pi(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}}),\qquad x_{\sigma_{n}}\sim p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}}),\qquad I_{n}:=I_{n-1}\cup\{\sigma_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,\ldots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,\ldots,D</annotation></semantics></math>,
where we abuse the notation to simplify <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{n}\}\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{n}\}\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random permutation of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,\ldots,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,\ldots,D)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us write <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x},\bm{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x},\bm{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> be the joint distribution of
<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{n})_{n=1}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{n})_{n=1}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> (the latter is constrained to be a permutation).
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x},\bm{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x},\bm{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(x_{\sigma_{n}}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(x_{\sigma_{n}}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})\right)\left(\prod_{n=1}^{D}p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(x_{\sigma_{n}}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})\right)=q_{\text{data}}(\bm{x})\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})\right)\left(\prod_{n=1}^{D}p_{\sigma_{n}|I_{n-1}}(x_{\sigma_{n}}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})\right)=q_{\text{data}}(\bm{x})\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">from the assumption <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j|I}=q_{j|I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j|I}=q_{j|I}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, it suffices to prove that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{\sigma}}\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{\sigma}}\prod_{n=1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, let us prove the following for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,D</annotation></semantics></math> by induction on <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>
(the case <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=D</annotation></semantics></math> is what we would like to prove ultimately):</span></p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})=1\qquad\text{for any $I_{D-k}$ with $\lvert I_{D-k}\rvert=D-k$
and $\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}}$}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></munder><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>for any </mtext><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> with </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})=1\qquad\text{for any $I_{D-k}$ with $\lvert I_{D-k}\rvert=D-k$
and $\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}}$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">It is clearly true for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is just the total probability sum
of the probability distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{D-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{D-1}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,
from the induction hypothesis, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1}}\pi(\sigma_{D-k+1}|\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}})\underbrace{\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+2},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})}_{=1\ \text{by induction hypothesis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>by induction hypothesis</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1}}\pi(\sigma_{D-k+1}|\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}})\underbrace{\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+2},\ldots,\sigma_{D}}\prod_{n=D-k+1}^{D}\pi(\sigma_{n}|\bm{x}_{I_{n-1}})}_{=1\ \text{by induction hypothesis}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1}}\pi(\sigma_{D-k+1}|\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}})=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\sigma_{D-k+1}}\pi(\sigma_{D-k+1}|\bm{x}_{I_{D-k}})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the proof has been completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 Balancing exploration and exploitation ‣ 4 Towards more efficient choose-then-sample algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By using the chain rule of KL divergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover &amp; Thomas, 2006</a>, Theorem 2.5.3)</cite>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\,\|\,p_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\,\|\,p_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">which shows the first inequality in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 Balancing exploration and exploitation ‣ 4 Towards more efficient choose-then-sample algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
Let us first consider the KL divergence between <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.
First, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log\Biggl(\prod_{i\in I}q_{i}(x_{i})\Biggr)+\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log\Biggl(\prod_{i\in I}q_{i}(x_{i})\Biggr)+\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}\sim q_{i}}\!\left[-\log q_{i}(x_{i})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}\sim q_{i}}\!\left[-\log q_{i}(x_{i})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in I}H(q_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in I}H(q_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by using a permutation <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>,
the remainder term of (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Proof of Equation ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) (entropy of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>)
can be rewritten as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{\sigma_{1}},\ldots,x_{\sigma_{k}}}\prod_{j=1}^{k}q_{\sigma_{j}|I_{j-1}}(x_{\sigma_{j}}|\bm{x}_{I_{j-1}})\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{\sigma_{1}},\ldots,x_{\sigma_{k}}}\prod_{j=1}^{k}q_{\sigma_{j}|I_{j-1}}(x_{\sigma_{j}}|\bm{x}_{I_{j-1}})\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\sum_{x_{\sigma_{1}},\ldots,x_{\sigma_{\ell}}}q_{I_{\ell-1}}(\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})(-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\sum_{x_{\sigma_{1}},\ldots,x_{\sigma_{\ell}}}q_{I_{\ell-1}}(\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})(-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}\sim q_{I_{\ell-1}}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{\sigma_{\ell}}\sim q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}}\!\left[-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}\sim q_{I_{\ell-1}}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{\sigma_{\ell}}\sim q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}}\!\left[-\log q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(x_{\sigma_{\ell}}|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}\sim q_{I_{\ell-1}}}\!\left[H(q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}\sim q_{I_{\ell-1}}}\!\left[H(q_{\sigma_{\ell}|I_{\ell-1}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I_{\ell-1}}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let us consider taking the average of the right-hand side over all the permutations.
With the uniformly random permutation <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>,
for each <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}=i</annotation></semantics></math> takes the uniformly distribution over <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[k]</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\ell-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\ell-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (conditioned by <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>) then takes the uniform distribution over
all the possible size-<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell-1)</annotation></semantics></math> subsets of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\setminus\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\setminus\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, if we write such an <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\sigma^{-1}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\sigma^{-1}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>,
the probability that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\subset I\setminus\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\subset I\setminus\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\sigma^{-1}(i)-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\sigma^{-1}(i)-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
can be computed as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\frac{1}{k}}_{\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sigma^{-1}(i)-1=\lvert J\rvert\right)}\binom{k-1}{\lvert J\rvert}^{-1}=\varphi(J|I\setminus\{i\})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.491em;" width="0.491em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\frac{1}{k}}_{\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sigma^{-1}(i)-1=\lvert J\rvert\right)}\binom{k-1}{\lvert J\rvert}^{-1}=\varphi(J|I\setminus\{i\}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability distribution defined just before (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 Balancing exploration and exploitation ‣ 4 Towards more efficient choose-then-sample algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
By applying this to (<a href="#A3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Proof of Equation ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>),
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]=\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{J\sim\varphi(\cdot|I\setminus\{i\})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{J}\sim q_{J}}\!\left[H(q_{i|J}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{J}))\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[-\log q_{I}(\bm{x}_{I})\right]=\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{J\sim\varphi(\cdot|I\setminus\{i\})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{J}\sim q_{J}}\!\left[H(q_{i|J}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{J}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining it with (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Proof of Equation ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>),
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})=\sum_{i\in I}H(q_{i})-\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{J\sim\varphi(\cdot|I\setminus\{i\})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{J}\sim q_{J}}\!\left[H(q_{i|J}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{J}))\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I}\,\|\,p_{I})=\sum_{i\in I}H(q_{i})-\sum_{i\in I}\mathbb{E}_{J\sim\varphi(\cdot|I\setminus\{i\})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{J}\sim q_{J}}\!\left[H(q_{i|J}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{J}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, for the remaining term,
it suffices to prove</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\,\|\,p_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right]\leq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}H(q_{i|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I})\,\|\,p_{I^{c}|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right]\leq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{I}\sim q_{I}}\!\left[\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}H(q_{i|I}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{I}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">This can be proven by using the positivity of entropy
and modifying (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Proof of Equation ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>),
with <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\cdot|I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\cdot|I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> be the event under which we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\Omega_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\bigl(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\Omega_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\bigl(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\in[N]_{&lt;k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\in[N]_{&lt;k}</annotation></semantics></math>, under <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}-\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now we want to estimate the ratio between
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>.
From Hölder’s inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}=S\cdot\frac{1}{S}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)^{\beta}\geq S\left(\frac{1}{S}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)\right)^{\beta}=S^{1-\beta}=S^{-1/\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}=S\cdot\frac{1}{S}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)^{\beta}\geq S\left(\frac{1}{S}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}(x)\right)^{\beta}=S^{1-\beta}=S^{-1/\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">By using this, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}\leq\frac{(k-1)}{(N-k+1)S^{-{1/\alpha}}}=\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{i\in I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}\leq\frac{(k-1)}{(N-k+1)S^{-{1/\alpha}}}=\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">By applying this to (<a href="#A3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), under <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}&gt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, by using (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>),
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\Omega_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\Omega_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3\epsilon^{2}}{8}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof of the proposition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Whether or not (<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) holds only depends on the actual values of <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we can define the set <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}\subset\mathcal{S}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}\subset\mathcal{S}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
(<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) is satisfied if and only if
<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now, let <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we have (recall <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{\ell}^{*}=i_{\ell}\mid i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{\ell-1}^{*}=i_{\ell-1},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}p_{i}(x_{i})^{1/\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(x_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We thus have <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}N\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{-1/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">follows from <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\prime}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the independence of <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j_{\ell}^{*})_{\ell=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j_{\ell}^{*})_{\ell=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#Thmsett2" title="Setting B (Moment sampler). ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Setting</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{j_{\ell}^{*}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((y_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\mid j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((y_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}\mid j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{P}\!\left(y_{i_{\ell}}=z_{i_{\ell}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\mathbb{P}\!\left(y_{i_{\ell}}=z_{i_{\ell}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\right)=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{\lVert p_{i_{\ell}}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">by letting <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}=\log\lVert\mu_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}=\log\lVert\mu_{i}\rVert_{\beta}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Proposition 1 (Gumbel-top-𝑘 trick, , , Eq. 18). ‣ 3 MaskGIT sampler secretly conducts temperature sampling ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
We obtain (<a href="#A2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proposition 6. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) through these two identities.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmthm7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By introducing extra variables, let us define</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k},(x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}=(z_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}\!\left(j_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,j_{k}^{*}=i_{k},(y_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k}=(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k},(x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}=(z_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we suppose <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are sampled independently.
These define probability distributions over <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]^{k}\times\mathcal{S}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]^{k}\times\mathcal{S}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From the independence and <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}=(z_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i_{\ell}})_{\ell=1}^{k})\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}=(z_{i})_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}p_{i}(z_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{\beta}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}p_{i}(z_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>
and recall the set <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
For <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From the definition of <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have (recall <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\!\left(i_{1}^{*}=i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}^{*}=i_{k}\mid(x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}=(z_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}p_{i}(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\prod_{\ell=1}^{k}\frac{p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})^{1/\alpha}\cdot p_{i_{\ell}}(z_{i_{\ell}})}{\sum_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{\ell-1}}\lVert p_{i}\rVert^{\beta}_{\beta}}\prod_{i\in[N]\setminus I_{k}}p_{i}(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) in the last equality.
Let us next bound the total variation distance between <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us denote <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)_{+}:=\max\{0,a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)_{+}:=\max\{0,a\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In general, for probability distributions <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> over the same finite set <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(q(x)-p(x))_{+}=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))=1-1=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(q(x)-p(x))_{+}=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))=1-1=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for the total variation distance, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(p,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(p,q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\lvert p(x)-q(x)\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\lvert p(x)-q(x)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}+\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(q(x)-p(x))_{+}\right)=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}+\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(q(x)-p(x))_{+}\right)=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}(p(x)-q(x))_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">By using this, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{S}^{N}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}+\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}+\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})-\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z}))_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})+\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})+\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{\bm{z}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}}\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)+\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)+\mathbb{P}\!\left((x_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\not\in\mathcal{Z}_{\epsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">By applying <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ B.2 Strategy for formal proof of ‣ Appendix B Formal and informal derivation of moment sampler ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)+\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq\left(\left(1-\epsilon-\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)^{-k}-1\right)+\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta\leq\frac{1}{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta\leq\frac{1}{2k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta)^{-1}=1+\delta\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\delta^{n}\leq 1+\frac{\delta}{1-\frac{1}{2k}}=1+\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta)^{-1}=1+\delta\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\delta^{n}\leq 1+\frac{\delta}{1-\frac{1}{2k}}=1+\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-1)\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\leq\frac{k-1}{2k-1}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-1)\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\leq\frac{k-1}{2k-1}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\delta)^{-k}\leq\left(1+\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\delta)^{-k}\leq\left(1+\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+\sum_{n=1}^{k}\binom{k}{n}\left(\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+\sum_{n=1}^{k}\binom{k}{n}\left(\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1+k\cdot\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\sum_{n=1}^{k}\frac{(k-1)^{n-1}}{n!}\left(\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1+k\cdot\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\sum_{n=1}^{k}\frac{(k-1)^{n-1}}{n!}\left(\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1+k\cdot\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{m!}\left((k-1)\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1+k\cdot\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{m!}\left((k-1)\frac{2k\delta}{2k-1}\right)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+\frac{2k^{2}\sqrt{e}}{2k-1}\delta&lt;1+4k\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>e</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+\frac{2k^{2}\sqrt{e}}{2k-1}\delta&lt;1+4k\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, assuming <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;\frac{1}{4k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}&lt;\frac{1}{4k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq 4k\left(\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)+\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})\leq 4k\left(\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\right)+\exp\left(-\frac{3}{8}\epsilon^{2}NS^{-1/\alpha}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">Since the total variation distance is always bounded by <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>,
actually
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) holds without the posed assumptions on <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon+\frac{(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that, when <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&lt;k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&lt;k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the upper bound of <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}(p_{\mathrm{moment}},p_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}(p_{\mathrm{moment}},p_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})</annotation></semantics></math> becomes larger than <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>,
which holds trivially true since <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above by <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
So, it suffices to prove the desired inequality with <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>log</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> under the assumption <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under this, by letting
<math id="A3.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{8}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{8}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
in (<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>),
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4k\sqrt{\frac{4}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}+\frac{4k(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}+\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4k\sqrt{\frac{4}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}+\frac{4k(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}+\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We need to make sure <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, but the above bound is valid even when <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,
again because of the boundedness of <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}\geq k^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq k^{2}\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert^{1/\alpha}\geq k^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4k(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\leq 4S^{1/\alpha}\cdot\frac{k^{2}-k}{N-k}\leq 4S^{1/\alpha}\cdot\frac{k^{2}}{N}=\frac{4k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\leq 4\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4k(k-1)S^{1/\alpha}}{N-k+1}\leq 4S^{1/\alpha}\cdot\frac{k^{2}-k}{N-k}\leq 4S^{1/\alpha}\cdot\frac{k^{2}}{N}=\frac{4k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\leq 4\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By applying this to (<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4k\sqrt{\frac{4}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}+5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4k\sqrt{\frac{4}{3}\frac{S^{1/\alpha}}{N}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}+5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(5+\sqrt{\frac{64}{3}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(5+\sqrt{\frac{64}{3}\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(1+\sqrt{\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 5\sqrt{\frac{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}{N}}\left(1+\sqrt{\log\frac{N}{k^{2}S^{1/\alpha}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by denoting <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}({p}_{\mathrm{moment}},{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{TV}}({p}_{\mathrm{moment}},{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\lvert{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\lvert{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\left\lvert\sum_{(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{N-k}}({p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}))\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\left\lvert\sum_{(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{N-k}}({p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}))\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\sum_{(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{N-k}}\lvert{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}))\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>moment</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\bm{i}\in[N]^{k}}\sum_{(z_{i})_{i\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{k}}\sum_{(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}\in\mathcal{S}^{N-k}}\lvert{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I})-{p}_{\mathrm{moment}}(\bm{i},(z_{i})_{i\in I},(z_{j})_{j\not\in I}))\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>moment</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>MaskGIT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d_{\mathrm{TV}}(\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{moment}},\tilde{p}_{\mathrm{MaskGIT}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">By combining this with (<a href="#A3.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>),
we obtain the desired conclusion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional experimental details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Sampling schedule</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of positions (so <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\mathcal{S}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\mathcal{S}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>)
and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of total sampling steps.
Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{n}\subset[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{n}\subset[D]</annotation></semantics></math> be the (random) set of indices that are open after the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th step,
i.e., <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset=J_{0}\subset J_{1}\subset\cdots\subset J_{N}=[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊂</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⊂</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset=J_{0}\subset J_{1}\subset\cdots\subset J_{N}=[D]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}:=J_{n}\setminus J_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}:=J_{n}\setminus J_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is the (random) set of indices we unmask at the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th step.
In all the experiments,
the cardinalities <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert J_{n}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert J_{n}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert I_{n}\rvert\ (=\lvert J_{n}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:0.889em;" width="0.889em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert I_{n}\rvert\ (=\lvert J_{n}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert)</annotation></semantics></math>
are predetermined by the unmasking size schedule such as:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cosine schedule: <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert J_{n}\rvert=\text{round}(\cos(\frac{\pi}{2}D(1-\frac{n}{N})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>round</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert J_{n}\rvert=\text{round}(\cos(\frac{\pi}{2}D(1-\frac{n}{N})))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uniform schedule: <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert J_{n}\rvert=\text{round}(D\cdot\frac{n}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>round</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert J_{n}\rvert=\text{round}(D\cdot\frac{n}{N})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, “round” means integer rounding.
We adopted the cosine schedule for image and the uniform schedule for language.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us now consider specifically the <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th sampling step out of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps.
Given the denoising model <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>,
we use the marginal distributions <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i|J_{n-1}})_{i\in[D]\setminus J_{n-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i|J_{n-1}})_{i\in[D]\setminus J_{n-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for this step.
Let <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of indices to unmask in this step, determined by the unmasking size schedule.
Then, for the sampler <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MaskGIT</span>, we use <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{OneRoundMaskGIT}((p_{i|J_{n-1}})_{i\in[D]\setminus J_{n-1}},k,\alpha_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>OneRoundMaskGIT</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{OneRoundMaskGIT}((p_{i|J_{n-1}})_{i\in[D]\setminus J_{n-1}},k,\alpha_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#alg1" title="In Appendix A Algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
to determine <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{I_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{I_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Gumbel temperature for the <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th step, which is scheduled as
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n}=\alpha(1-n/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n}=\alpha(1-n/N)</annotation></semantics></math> following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature parameter of the method presented in the figures (e.g., <a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5.1 Image modeling ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
We use the same <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Moment</span> (<a href="#alg2" title="In Appendix A Algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and its variants
given the parameter <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that, in the final step (<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=N</annotation></semantics></math>) of <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Moment</span> or other temperature-sampling methods,
we omit the sampling temperature (or take <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), in order that it corresponds to the final step of <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MaskGIT</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Partial caching</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the partial caching algorithm we described in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Partial caching approximation with transformers ‣ 4 Towards more efficient choose-then-sample algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>,
we have a degree of freedom in dividing the selected index set <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>
(where we have<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\cup B=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\cup B=I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\cap B=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\cap B=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us explain our implementation.
Let us use the notation of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> introduced in the previous section.
In the <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th step,
suppose we decompose <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of indices unmasked in the intermediate step of partial caching.
If we let <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{n-1/2}:=J_{n-1}\cup A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{n-1/2}:=J_{n-1}\cup A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
then we adopted the canonical extension of the scheduler in <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Sampling schedule ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cosine schedule: <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert=\text{round}(\cos(\frac{\pi}{2}D(1-\frac{n-1/2}{N})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>round</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert=\text{round}(\cos(\frac{\pi}{2}D(1-\frac{n-1/2}{N})))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uniform schedule: <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert=\text{round}(D\cdot\frac{n-1/2}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>round</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert=\text{round}(D\cdot\frac{n-1/2}{N})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the cardinality of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> was determined by <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert A_{n}\rvert=\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert A_{n}\rvert=\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on the sampling schedule we use.
Since each of our sampling algorithm outputs an ordering of masked indices
(from which we determine <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>),
we simply determine <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as the top-<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> of the ordered indices (<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\lvert A_{n}\rvert=\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\lvert A_{n}\rvert=\lvert J_{n-1/2}\rvert-\lvert J_{n-1}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Computational efficiency of partial caching</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total cost of <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">attention computation</span>
in partial caching is <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\lvert I\rvert/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\lvert I\rvert/D</annotation></semantics></math> times the original full attention computation (in terms of the notations in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Partial caching approximation with transformers ‣ 4 Towards more efficient choose-then-sample algorithms ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
However, it costs more computation in caching the vectors and other CPU/GPU operations.
Indeed, while caching shows some performance gain with A6000 latency in the language experiment
(<a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5.1 Image modeling ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, Right),
it vanishes when we use H100 GPU (<a href="#A4.F6" title="In D.4 Additional details on language modeling experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, Right).
It would be caused by the faster attention computation of H100, reducing
its weight among the overall computational cost and making other computational overhead apparent.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Additional details on image modeling experiments</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MAGE ViT-B model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, which we used in the experiments,
can be regarded as a masked diffusion model
on the space of a pretrained VQGAN tokenizers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Esser et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
It was trained on the ImageNet <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2009</a>)</cite>.
The codebook size is given by <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert=1024</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the length of each token sequence (corresponding to a single image) is <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=256</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each experiment with MAGE was conducted with a single A6000 GPU with a minibatch size of 64.
Based on 50000 unconditional images generated from each sampler,
we measured FID and IS against the ImageNet dataset
by using <span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch-fidelity<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">2</span></span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/toshas/torch-fidelity" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://github.com/toshas/torch-fidelity</a><span id="footnote2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">.</span></span></span></span></span>,
following the description of the repository of MAGE<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/LTH14/mage" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/LTH14/mage</a>.</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Additional details on language modeling experiments</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the SDTT model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deschenaux &amp; Gulcehre, 2025</a>)</cite><span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            It was loaded by
<span id="footnote4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">load_small_student(loss="kld", round=7)</span>
in the repository <a href="https://github.com/jdeschena/sdtt" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/jdeschena/sdtt</a>.</span></span></span>,
which is a masked diffusion model over a GPT-2 tokenizers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.
It was trained on the OpenWebText dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gokaslan &amp; Cohen, 2019</a>)</cite>.
The codebook size is <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert=50257" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>50257</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\mathcal{S}\rvert=50257</annotation></semantics></math>
and the token sequence length is given by <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
Most experiments were conducted on a single H100 GPU,
while the preliminary experiments, the ones in <a href="#A4.SS4.SSS1" title="D.4.1 Numerical precision ‣ D.4 Additional details on language modeling experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4.1</span></a>,
and the latency computation in <a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5.1 Image modeling ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(Right) were conducted on a single A6000 GPU.
Each plot was computed by 1024 samples
generated with a minibatch size of <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>, using the following performance metrics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generative Perplexity.</span>
It was measured against the GPT-2 large model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2019</a>)</cite>
and averaged over 1024 samples.
We used the implementation of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deschenaux &amp; Gulcehre (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy.</span>
Following the existing work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gat et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>,
we measured the sentence-wise entropy for checking the diversity
of generated sentences.
In our implementation (following the description of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>),
for a sequence of tokens <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{D})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we define the sentence entropy as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}\cap\bm{x}}\frac{\#\{i\in[D]\mid x_{i}=s\}}{D}\log\frac{\#\{i\in[D]\mid x_{i}=s\}}{D}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}\cap\bm{x}}\frac{\#\{i\in[D]\mid x_{i}=s\}}{D}\log\frac{\#\{i\in[D]\mid x_{i}=s\}}{D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\cap\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\cap\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of tokens appearing in <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Its average over 1024 samples was plotted.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.F6" title="In D.4 Additional details on language modeling experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>(Left) shows the omitted results for Generative Perplexity.
While the methods with lower temperature apparently attain better the generation quality,
lowering the temperature extremely harms the diversity in reality (<a href="#S5.F5" title="In 5.1 Image modeling ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, Left).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04525v1/ppl_vs_steps.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:226/151;" width="226" height="151"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04525v1/h100_perplexity_vs_time_with_error_log.svg" id="A4.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:226/151;" width="226" height="151"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>
Additional experimental results.
(<span id="A4.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Left</span>) Generative Perplexity of various samplers with temperature sampling.
(<span id="A4.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Right</span>) Generative Perplexity of our proposed samplers against sampling time per batch on H100 GPU.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.1 </span>Numerical precision</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2025)</a></cite> pointed out that the sampling from masked diffusion models
with low numerical precision (32-bit)
can lead to errors in categorical sampling,
showing lower (better) Generative Perplexity at the cost of lower (worse) Entropy.
Because of this, they suggest using 64-bit computation for a fair evaluation of masked diffusion models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, as they also note in Section J.2.2 of their paper,
it is primarily because the lower numerical precision results in biased positional selection
rather than the sampling distribution shift at each position.
In our case,
since we fix the token positions in most samplers (except <span id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MaskGIT</span>),
we do not suffer from this problem though we use 32-bit precision.
Indeed, <a href="#A4.T1" title="In D.4.1 Numerical precision ‣ D.4 Additional details on language modeling experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that,
while the vanilla sampler in discrete diffusion suffer from the difference in numerical precision,
<span id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Fixed</span>, which corresponds to <span id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Random</span> in the main text, exhibits similar results
in both precision settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Comparison of different numerical precision in <span id="A4.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Vanilla</span>
and <span id="A4.T1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Fixed</span> samplers.
<span id="A4.T1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Vanilla</span> is a standard sampler for discrete diffusion,
where it independently determines whether or not unmasking a certain position.
<span id="A4.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Fixed</span> is a sampler that pre-determines the number of unmasked positions at each step,
and it determines which positions to unmask uniformly at random.
Both follows the uniform schedule (<a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Sampling schedule ‣ Appendix D Additional experimental details ‣ Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond: Adaptive Order Selection in Masked Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) in expectation.
</figcaption>
